==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Bailiff (Channel Islands)}}
===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno}} and {{etyl|fro}} {{term|bailif|lang=fro}} (plural {{term|bailis}}), {{etyl|LL.}} {{recons|baiulivus|bāiulivus|lang=LL.|sc=Latn}}. Compare Modern French {{term|bailli|lang=fr}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|bāʹ-lĭf}}, {{IPA|/ˈbeɪlɪf/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"beIlIf/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{legal}} A legal [[officer]] to whom some degree of [[authority]], care or [[jurisdiction]] is committed.
# {{British}} The [[steward]] or [[overseer]] of an [[estate]].
# {{Channel Islands}} the [[Chief Justice]] in each of the [[Channel Islands|Channel Island]] [[bailiwick]]s of [[Jersey]] and [[Guernsey]], also serving as president of the legislature and having ceremonial and executive functions
#* The '''Bailiff''' of Jersey is the President of the States and acts as Speaker of the Assembly in the Westminster tradition. He is responsible for the orderly conduct of the States Assembly and its business. As Presiding Officer he has the right of speech – which is mainly exercised for ensuring the orderly conduct of the proceedings – but he cannot vote.
#*: {{quote-web | date = 2011-06-29 | title = The Bailiff of Jersey | site = States Assembly | url = http://www.statesassembly.gov.je/about/history/Pages/BailiffJersey.aspx| accessdate = 2013-03-03 }}

